; Redefinition — edit live code without splitting the session
; Same-type body edits update the existing callable; guarded edits either
; publish whole or leave the earlier definition untouched.

; A small call chain. total calls price through its live callable slot:

(defn price [:Int n] (* n 3))
(defn total [:Int n] (price (+ n 1)))
(total 9)

; This body-only edit keeps price's language type. total needs no rebuild;
; its next call reaches the new body:

(defn price [:Int n] (* n 4))
(total 9)

; A type-changing edit has a direct committed dependent, so it is rejected
; before publication. The diagnostic names the target, both types, total,
; and the remedy — retain the old type or use a new name:

(defn price [:String label] (str label "!"))

; Rejected means the old definition is still the one the session calls:

(total 9)
price

; With no blocking dependent, a type-changing edit can replace the callable
; atomically. Later calls see only the new type and body:

(defn label [:Int n] (show n))
(defn label [:String text] (str text "!"))
(label "gold")

; Live edits stay coherent: a successful edit is fully published, and a
; rejected one leaves the working definition in place.
